WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.844
This episode focuses on ACS period estimates.

2
00:00:02.844 --> 00:00:11.122
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:11.122 --> 00:00:15.104
ACS one-year and five-year products measure periods of different length.

4
00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:19.362
A one-year estimate uses twelve months of collected data and favors currency.

5
00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:25.500
A five-year estimate combines sixty months, offers broader geographic coverage, and generally favors precision.

6
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.775
The five-year label names the final year, but the estimate does not describe that date alone.

7
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:33.158
It describes the entire collection period.

8
00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:38.603
Do not call it a rolling average unless the specific statistic and method justify that language.

9
00:00:38.603 --> 00:00:42.288
Compare like products and nonoverlapping periods when possible.

10
00:00:42.288 --> 00:00:46.500
A one-year estimate and a five-year estimate are not direct substitutes.

11
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.876
Product choice should follow geography, precision needs, and the decision's tolerance for older observations.

12
00:00:52.876 --> 00:00:54.621
Torrance application segment.

13
00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:58.892
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

14
00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:06.532
The cited City of Torrance primary source is About Torrance, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/About-Torrance.

15
00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:14.473
For a local analysis, date every local fact and avoid comparing a current City count directly with a multi-year ACS period estimate.

16
00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:22.956
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

17
00:01:22.956 --> 00:01:32.793
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

18
00:01:32.793 --> 00:01:35.991
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

19
00:01:35.991 --> 00:01:40.699
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

20
00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:44.923
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

21
00:01:44.923 --> 00:01:50.837
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

22
00:01:50.837 --> 00:01:55.122
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
